<!--Post: 8216--><!--Time: 1109005254-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8216"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ztargate<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ztargate<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 21, 2005 - 9:00 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Finally I find a clear picture of what was eating at me for weeks. That postmark next to the stamp on BTK&#39;s two communications.  <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.downingworld.com/postmark.jpg" target=_top>http://www.downingworld.com/postmark.jpg</a> <BR> <BR>Someone posted it in the resource section of this website. Thanks to whoever did. <BR> <BR>Now my question is... <BR> <BR>This is a postmark that is very old. So, how did it get to the postcards he mailed in February 2005? <BR> <BR>Did he reconstructed them from old mail? Did he really work for the post office and stole it from his work decades ago? <BR> <BR>Can someone come up with a better explanation? <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.geocities.com/for_btk_board/postcardcartoon1.jpg" target=_top>http://www.geocities.com/for_btk_board/postcardcar toon1.jpg</a> <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.geocities.com/for_btk_board/postcardcartoon2.jpg" target=_top>http://www.geocities.com/for_btk_board/postcardcar toon2.jpg</a><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8216-->
<!--Post: 8217--><!--Time: 1109005754-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8217"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Amandab<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Amandab<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 21, 2005 - 9:09 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I don&#39;t understand; that looks like it&#39;s plugging the new movie &#34;Robots&#34; - am I msising something?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8217-->
<!--Post: 8220--><!--Time: 1109006928-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8220"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Iq<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Iq<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 21, 2005 - 9:28 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Z- <BR> <BR>I don&#39;t think the postmark is old at all. Rodney and Fender are characters in the new movie &#34;robots&#34;. What made you think it was old? <BR> <BR>iq<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8220-->
<!--Post: 8240--><!--Time: 1109012255-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8240"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Jed4258<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Jed4258<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 21, 2005 - 10:57 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Just checked the USPS site, this is a promotional stamp <BR><a href="http://www.usps.com/cpim/ftp/bulletin/2005/pb22147.pdf" target=_top>http://www.usps.com/cpim/ftp/bulletin/2005/pb22147 .pdf</a> <BR>Page 65 <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8240-->
<!--Post: 8242--><!--Time: 1109012534-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8242"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tecno242<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tecno242<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 21, 2005 - 11:02 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->It&#39;s slightly interesting that one of them originated in St. Paul Minnesota.  <BR> <BR>I&#39;ve seen lots of links to Minnesota or Detroit being a second stomping ground for BTK.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8242-->
<!--Post: 8243--><!--Time: 1109012881-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8243"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Amandab<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Amandab<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 21, 2005 - 11:08 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Why Detroit?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8243-->
<!--Post: 8255--><!--Time: 1109016099-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8255"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Iq<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Iq<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 21, 2005 - 12:01 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Tecno- <BR> <BR>I don&#39;t believe any of the actual letters originated anywhere other than Wichita.  <BR>The link above is just an example that provides a clear picture of the postmark. <BR> <BR>iq<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8255-->
<!--Post: 8259--><!--Time: 1109018927-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8259"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ztargate<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ztargate<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 21, 2005 - 12:48 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I assumed is it old, because it said so in the website it linked to. The link is on catchbtk.com&#39;s resource page, I didn&#39;t post it there. <BR> <BR>I am not implying that BTK&#39;s letters originated in Minnesota. The picture shows the stamp from Minnesota because it is clearer. The ones on BTK&#39;s postcards are very fuzzy. <BR> <BR>I am not familiar with the movie Robots, but I guess I&#39;m gonna have to watch it now, eh? <BR> <BR>Thanks for letting me know about the movie. See? This things are under my very nose and I don&#39;t see them. Let&#39;s see, I spent about a week trying to figure out what the drawing next to the stamp on the cards was. Now I know. <BR> <BR>The question now is... does Wichita post offices use that same type of stamp? <BR><IMG SRC="http://www.catchbtk.com/discus/clipart/happy.gif" ALT=":-&#41;" BORDER=0><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8259-->
<!--Post: 8284--><!--Time: 1109038070-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8284"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Sidewalker<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Sidewalker<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 21, 2005 - 6:07 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I work for the Postal Service. Many different types of cancellation marks are used. I remember the Christmas one several yrs ago, which had a Dr Suess cancellation on it seeming like a promotion for the movie The Grinch. <BR>Different areas use different cancellation marks, for different things. In my area, a large chunk of the bay area uses one type cancellation mark. But if say, there was maybe a new postoffice bldg, or some commerative thing happening, they may use a special cancellation mark.  I&#39;ll have to pay attention to some of the cancellation marks, just to see. <BR>&#40;I know, they had several for Valentines day, recently&#41;<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8284-->
<!--Post: 8344--><!--Time: 1109080227-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8344"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rev<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rev<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 22, 2005 - 5:50 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I wouldn&#39;t waste my time looking too much into this cancellation mark.  It is on all mail coming from Wichita.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8344-->
<!--Post: 8658--><!--Time: 1109272881-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8658"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Suze<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Suze<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 24, 2005 - 11:21 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Ztargate, The second link you posted &#40;above&#41; Happ Kakemann Postcard with the robot circled...I understand the cancellation mark is from the P.O.... but if you go further over and look at the stamp...there is a label outlined on the stamp ...do you know what this is?  <BR> <BR>If you print a copy it is much more noticable &#40;on photo paper even better&#41;. All of BTK&#39;s mailings have a label outline around his return address etc.   <BR> <BR>Has something been superimposed over the stamp?  Or could this be something the police did...labeling it as evidence?  Any ideas?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8658-->
<!--Post: 8696--><!--Time: 1109291045-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8696"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ztargate<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ztargate<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 24, 2005 - 4:24 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I think it&#39;s all part of the cancellation stamp. But, it may be something else someone added.  <BR> <BR>The pictures are in such terrible shape, I wish there were official copies which were clear and neat. That way we could be able to see stuff on them. <BR> <BR><IMG SRC="http://www.catchbtk.com/discus/clipart/happy.gif" ALT=":-&#41;" BORDER=0><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8696-->
